      id: "vault-tloas-taylors-advice-to-sombr-on-hate-comments-a-privilege-to-be-r",
      slug: "showgirl-sombr-taylor-advice-hate-comments",
      date: "2026-09-23",
      dateLabel: "September 23, 2026",
      title: "Taylor’s advice to sombr on hate comments: “a privilege to be receiving these”",
      summary: "Asked by Elle for the best advice he had ever gotten, the 21-year-old sombr — the singer Taylor hand-picked to cover her songs at her Songwriters Hall of Fame induction — went straight to “the person I look up to most” and her counsel on online hate: if it ever stops, maybe you have slipped from your peak.",
      body: ["Asked by Elle (published Sept. 23, 2026) for the best advice he had ever been given, the 21-year-old singer-songwriter sombr went straight to Taylor: “The person I look up to most has given me. The amazing pop star.” Her counsel was about living with online hate as his profile climbed — reframe it as a scoreboard rather than a wound. In his telling, the lesson ran: “if these hate comments go away, maybe you’re not at your peak anymore. I think it’s a privilege to be receiving these and rise above it.”", "He added that time had changed how he answers critics at all. A younger sombr, thrust into the spotlight as a teenager, once felt the pull to defend himself; he said he “wouldn’t respond now,” having learned that reacting tends to make things worse.", "The exchange is the latest beat in a friendship that started the way many of his heroes’ do — Taylor praised him in an interview, he sent a thank-you note, and she wrote back with a letter and a necklace. At her June 2026 Songwriters Hall of Fame induction she had asked the then-20-year-old to open her segment with covers of “Cardigan” and “Dear John” in place of a performance of her own, calling him “the future.” The advice on hate reads as an extension of that mentorship: a veteran of nearly two decades of public scrutiny handing a rising artist a way to carry it."],
      tags: ["Music"],
      images: [{ url: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/Sombr%2C_Islington_Academy%2C_London_%28cropped%29.jpg", credit: "Drew de F Fawkes, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons", caption: "sombr performing in London in 2025 — the rising singer-songwriter Taylor has mentored since praising him in an interview.", kind: "archival", focalPoint: "50% 30%" }],
